{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/verification.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:34:34.165824Z","id":"7081ac09c683ef93c85d3b251d305fb9141ee4180cbe604b224348fe9b1ef900","body":{"detail":"§10.1 drives a real `claude -p` with this branch's plugin against a scratch daemon and a scripted Messages API that calls the publish tool, then replies as a LAN viewer with curl and validates the export with Ajv. Unlike scripts/smoke-claude-ask.sh, its fake model (a variant of scripts/fake-anthropic.py whose first turn calls `mcp__plugin_clax_clax__publish`) and its driver were not committed, so the check is described, not rerunnable as is. A scripts/smoke-claude-toolpath.sh, reusing fake-anthropic.py with a publish scenario, would make it repeatable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1085},"end":{"line":1100},"content_hash":"2a2bc6f18be95108c6873fc23dd7f10d97f1cebac973297f961d3f8979d1de8b"},"summary":"The Toolpath manual check (§10.1) has no script in the repository","tags":["verification","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.811733Z","id":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","body":{"detail":"Added for the shell: participants agents' name and person ({public_id, name, owner}); a thread owner's person_name; a thread's approves_first (public IDs, null for the owner; browsers only, absent when empty); and owner: true on GET /api/viewers/me and the artifact boot payload's viewer for the owner's browser. Agents' payloads change only by the name and person keys spec 2026-10-08 section 19 item 6 allows.","kind":"concern","summary":"The contract does not yet describe the fields the Send menu and owner chip read","tags":["task:24","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:42.668690Z","id":"35572e2274d3fc3b78b5fe674c391f6b9d2183a26a7f9d6a0c39d06971a1e776","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","summary":"Since bb547990: thread views no longer carry approves_first; the new browser-only route GET /api/artifacts/{aid}/approves-first?threads=<tid,…> answers {approves_first: [public ID | null]} (403 for LAN viewers, anonymous callers and agents; 404 for a thread of another artifact; at most 200 threads). Question views and inbox items' agent gain name; browsers get people's names as stored, agents the payload-safe form.","tags":["task:24","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319721Z","id":"d74a29be48f8826b30999dbe3bf8a9e7486f491197c67db70c9b595700e55335","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs (the status tool's annotations) changed status to read_only_hint false, destructive false, idempotent true, because `name` writes. Under Codex's `writes` approval mode (crates/clax-cli/src/codex_approvals.rs:12) a tool not annotated readOnlyHint asks, so status, which ran unasked, now prompts; docs/contract.md:56 still says readOnlyHint true.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"966a28b85777889409a04e068b00adbd01e067425963e6aedf0515c1a43859cb"},"suggested_fix":"Move status to the destructiveHint false list in docs/contract.md and say there that `writes` mode asks for it.","summary":"The contract still lists status among the readOnlyHint tools, but status is now annotated read_only_hint = false","tags":["review","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.457198Z","id":"e104b84998514f5d815bba578eba18ce20226e26f2a33019af423d45e7df973d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"The contract now lists status as not read-only (destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true) because it names the agent with `name`, and comments_handoff among the state-changing tools (7a06e2cd).","supersedes":"d74a29be48f8826b30999dbe3bf8a9e7486f491197c67db70c9b595700e55335","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:07:31.464183Z","id":"b49fdc77c91f68d06fd9447da725617e40cffcd4fe5b5b544b833edd4aa66d67","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28338345","summary":"docs/contract.md now describes them (28338345): participants' agents carry name and person {public_id, name, owner} ('Versions, seen marks and attention'); a thread's owner {handle, name, person, live, person_name} ('Thread ownership'); GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/approves-first?threads= and who learns it ('Approvals'); owner: true on GET /api/viewers/me and the boot payload's viewer ('Security model'); the question view's and inbox item's agent name. grep -n 'approves-first?threads\\|person_name}' docs/contract.md finds them.","supersedes":"06d36deac10389c296e42470276d7a5f535689b98d1be753d0be1f645f583d9d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.539101Z","id":"a212e22cc55dcf1dbcad7306fd3b81d0fa56aa37c0136d878bb92518f3f05cec","body":{"detail":"The text line is as written, but the tool result's withheld entry is {thread_id, artifact_id, count, asked: false, no_access: true} (docs/contract.md:122-123; crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs Placeholder; asserted in rows_on_an_artifact_the_session_may_not_read_are_held_and_told_once). An agent sent a thread on an artifact before its first take, whose access then ends, learns that artifact's ID only from this entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3134},"end":{"line":3136},"content_hash":"4476c5f57c01898b3c87530d102614b68370d620a002bdce4e8dec9e39b7238e"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'the thread's and artifact's IDs and the count' here, or leave artifact_id out of no_access entries.","summary":"The contract says the lost-access notice carries the thread's ID and the count only; its withheld entry also carries the artifact ID","tags":["review","task:24","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:58:14.169491Z","id":"ec17c3b6a225aca6867dad990faa159ca2b8d567fd706a0a79a0a2e3b2ec8fe5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:73c2b8e3","summary":"Fixed: docs/contract.md says the session is told with the thread's and the artifact's IDs and the count only (the line names the thread; the withheld entry adds artifact_id), and names a removed raise among the causes.","supersedes":"a212e22cc55dcf1dbcad7306fd3b81d0fa56aa37c0136d878bb92518f3f05cec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594217Z","id":"f45591f71b69438e60aebfd7b4bf854ba4d1fb1d7492685b43dd4f4339c11dd3","body":{"detail":"docs/usage.md:367 says writes need the daemon token, \"so LAN viewers can read artifacts and comment on them but not publish or change them\". With people, a connected person's agents publish, reply, resolve and write documents with key-bound grants, and their browsers approve and narrow. The guide's Use section (docs/usage.md:126-166) lists no `clax connect`, `clax people`, `clax approvals` or `clax agents rename`, says nothing of People (/people) or approvals, and nowhere says \"use a trusted LAN: Clax traffic is not encrypted\" (spec 2026-10-08 O7, §21). Only the developer note at docs/usage.md:266 and docs/contract.md describe them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"6a597844d96b84358c643af87ae66b0c05a053a40d9f8cf9b0b466791212e432"},"suggested_fix":"Add a short \"Working with other people\" part to Use (invite, `clax connect`, People, approvals, the not-connected switch, trusted LAN only) and rewrite the security model paragraph for grants and signatures.","summary":"The user guide's security model says LAN viewers cannot publish or change anything, and the guide never explains connecting a second person","tags":["review","final-review-ui","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.305871Z","id":"52ec6e9f30f037d530b20b373fbe6a5ecee0323d788d66f764412335668f05c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:107d63a5","summary":"docs/usage.md: a People subsection in Use (invites, requests, after connecting, agents, approvals, viewers not connected, revoking), the CLI lines for clax connect, clax people, clax agents and clax approvals, and the security model rewritten for connected people's signed requests, browser-only approvals and rights, and 'Clax traffic on the LAN is not encrypted: serve on the LAN only on a network you trust'. Checked against docs/contract.md 'People and their agents', 'Approvals', 'Names' and 'Security model'.","supersedes":"f45591f71b69438e60aebfd7b4bf854ba4d1fb1d7492685b43dd4f4339c11dd3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/usage.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835131Z","id":"4bf9be8f14c9bb823e2fc299dc181992172fb8a6e19598a4440247c1aba1caaa","body":{"detail":"The prerequisite is Node 22, the Node MODULE.bazel pins for the web, Pi and browser checks and native-check.yml installs. demo/local.ts and crates/clax-worker's scripts (e2e*.mjs, test-wasm.mjs, deploy.mjs) use no API newer than Node 22; .ts scripts run by node rely on type stripping, unflagged from Node 22.18.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"5e4fd852a88daddd1c554f232f5b49da8d6ad99f6f093d825f6237e288cb4ef3"},"summary":"Node 26 for development","tags":["build","revisit:a hosted or demo script needs a Node API newer than 22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.074149Z","id":"5c91017d84e3ea75af5d567f8d3621c96e68fb604e89dacbff6620e1ef684a62","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1282 sets person = false for a resolved thread, so send_target (threads.rs:1196-1235) skips the handoff_target branch and returns unknown_agent ('no live agent on this artifact has that handle', or 'not an agent handle' for a name) before send_routed can answer thread_resolved. Only a to that already owns or watches the artifact reaches send_in's thread_resolved (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs send_in). The gallery dialog and CLI comments send --to (docs/contract.md 'comments send') would show the wrong reason. No test covers a resolved thread with a non-watching to.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1459},"end":{"line":1475},"content_hash":"64e56d14fb83e4a9415b80ede360b47e7b526392de3abb9f20e5ed3b2f5472b9"},"suggested_fix":"Check t.status == \"resolved\" in send() before send_target and return thread_resolved, or change the contract text; add a test either way.","summary":"Contract says a send naming a non-watching agent on a resolved thread is 400 thread_resolved; the daemon answers 400 unknown_agent","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/contract.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.567809Z","id":"6b20fa29e049ec6e1477c62637de9b1b03dd14da7b617edfae3df15f7a5d5730","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md:1470-1471 says 'a resolved thread 400 thread_resolved'. crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1281-1283 sets person = person && t.status != \"resolved\" before send_target; with person false, send_target (:1205-1234) skips the handoff_target branch for a to that is not a live watcher and returns 400 unknown_agent ('no live agent on this artifact has that handle' or 'not an agent handle') before send_routed (:1291) is reached. grep of crates/clax-server/tests/api_briefs.rs for thread_resolved finds no case.","kind":"comment","references":"5c91017d84e3ea75af5d567f8d3621c96e68fb604e89dacbff6620e1ef684a62","summary":"confirmed: a resolved thread naming a non-watching agent answers unknown_agent, not the contract's thread_resolved","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
